   <media:title>Stone Hunters | Boucheron</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/_jRpNiEUZ1E?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/_jRpNiEUZ1E/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>What does it take to find an exceptional colored stone? 

Boucheron’s new documentary follows Hélène Poulit-Duquesne and Claire Choisne on a journey in search of the world’s most remarkable gemstones. From Jaipur, India, to Tucson, USA, the duo of gemstone hunters meets partners and explores stones in every shade, seeking specimens that meet the Maison’s exacting standards of quality and sustainability.

Their quest is driven by expertise, but also by instinct. Beyond rarity and technical perfection, a stone must stir an emotion. Sometimes, amid hundreds of specimens, one immediately stands out - an unexpected color, a singular light, an inexplicable attraction. A journey into the fascinating world of colored stones, where expertise meets emotion, and where every encounter can inspire a new creation.</media:description>
